1
00:00:00,181 --> 00:00:01,285
(Q1) Good morning.

2
00:00:01,285 --> 00:00:02,314
Can I help you?

3
00:00:02,314 --> 00:00:02,869
Yes.

4
00:00:02,869 --> 00:00:10,155
[Example] I've just been accepted on a course at the university and I'd like to try and arrange accommodation in the hall of residence.

5
00:00:10,155 --> 00:00:11,318
Yes, certainly.

6
00:00:11,318 --> 00:00:12,936
Please sit down.

7
00:00:12,936 --> 00:00:17,835
What I'll do is fill in a form with you to find out a little more about your preferences and so forth.

8
00:00:17,835 --> 00:00:19,102
Thank you.

9
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:21,880
[Q1定位词：name原词] So first of all, can I take your name?

10
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,586
It's Anu Bhatt.

11
00:00:23,586 --> 00:00:25,302
Could you spell your name please?

12
00:00:25,302 --> 00:00:31,659
[Q1答案句] Yes. A-N-U…B-H-A double T. A-N-U……

13
00:00:31,659 --> 00:00:34,461
(Q2) Thanks, and could I ask your date of birth?

14
00:00:34,461 --> 00:00:37,749
[Q2答案句：注意日期写法，和字数要求（不需要写年份）] The 31st March 1972.

15
00:00:37,749 --> 00:00:38,806
Thank you.

16
00:00:38,806 --> 00:00:40,082
(Q3) [Q3定位词1️⃣： where... from = country of origin 来源国] And where are you from?

17
00:00:40,082 --> 00:00:41,166
India.

18
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:42,118
Oh right.

19
00:00:42,118 --> 00:00:44,222
[Q3临近定位词❗️：study原词， what ... study = course] And what will you be studying?

20
00:00:44,222 --> 00:00:46,702
[Q3答案句] I'm doing a course in nursing.

21
00:00:46,702 --> 00:00:48,037
Right, thank you.

22
00:00:48,037 --> 00:00:51,052
(Q4) And how long would you want to stay in hall, do you think?

23
00:00:51,052 --> 00:00:57,228
[Q4干扰项： 3     +    Q4答案句：2， 通过but得到] Well, it'll take three years but I'd only like to stay in hall for two.

24
00:00:57,228 --> 00:01:00,879
I'd like to think about living outside for the third year.

25
00:01:00,879 --> 00:01:04,334
(Q5) Fine. And what did you have in mind for catering?

26
00:01:04,334 --> 00:01:09,042
Do you want to cook for yourself or have all your meals provided, that's full board?

27
00:01:09,042 --> 00:01:11,440
Is there something in between?

28
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,042
Yes.

29
00:01:12,042 --> 00:01:15,548
[Q5定位词1️⃣: half board原词，继续跟] You can just have evening meal provided, which is half board.

30
00:01:15,548 --> 00:01:17,166
That's what I'd prefer.

31
00:01:17,166 --> 00:01:19,861
Yes a lot of students opt for that.

32
00:01:19,861 --> 00:01:24,676
[Q5核心定位词❗️： special原词， diet=dietary 饮食的] Now, with that in mind, do you have any special diet, anything we should know about?

33
00:01:24,676 --> 00:01:27,530
[Q5答案句： don't take 表否定+ no, 跟出答案词] Yes, I don't take red meat.

34
00:01:27,530 --> 00:01:29,379
No red meat.

35
00:01:29,379 --> 00:01:34,200
(Q6) Now, thinking about the room itself, we have a number of options.

36
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:37,750
You can have a single study bedroom or you can have a shared one.

37
00:01:37,750 --> 00:01:40,690
These are both what we call simple rooms.

38
00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:47,397
The other alternative is to opt for a single bedsit which actually has more space and better facilities.

39
00:01:47,397 --> 00:01:50,822
There's about 20 a week difference between them.

40
00:01:50,822 --> 00:01:56,933
[Q6答案句： 排除干扰后， 对话形式 要听「POI」 的] Well, actually my grant is quite generous and I think the bedsit sounds the best option.

41
00:01:56,933 --> 00:01:57,942
Lovely.

42
00:01:57,942 --> 00:02:01,192
I'll put you down for that and we'll see what availability is like.

43
00:02:01,192 --> 00:02:05,180
(Q7) Now can I ask some other personal details which we like to have on record?

44
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:06,488
Yes, of course.

45
00:02:06,488 --> 00:02:09,727
[Q7定位词： interests 原词] I wonder if you could let us know what your interests are.

46
00:02:09,727 --> 00:02:13,713
This might help us get a closer match for placing you in a particular hall.

47
00:02:13,713 --> 00:02:17,986
[Q7答案句] Ummm. Well, I love the theatre.

48
00:02:17,986 --> 00:02:18,776
Right.

49
00:02:18,776 --> 00:02:22,366
And I enjoy sports, particularly badmintion.

50
00:02:22,366 --> 00:02:24,022
That's worth knowing.

51
00:02:24,022 --> 00:02:33,814
(Q8) Now, what we finish with on the form is really a list from you of what your priorities are in choosing a hall and we'll do our best to take these into account.

52
00:02:33,814 --> 00:02:39,913
[Q8答案句： the first thing 表明「第一点」， other关键词原词，跟住] Well, the first thing is I'd prefer a hall where there are other mature students. If possible.

53
00:02:39,913 --> 00:02:43,598
Yes, we do have halls which tend to cater for slightly older students.

54
00:02:43,598 --> 00:02:48,841
(Q9) [and 表示递进，第二点。   Q9答案句： out of = outside] Ummm and I'd prefer to be out of town.

55
00:02:48,841 --> 00:02:53,464
That's actually very good for you because we tend to have more vacancies in out-of-town halls.

56
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:54,498
Lucky!

57
00:02:54,498 --> 00:02:55,580
Yes.

58
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:56,996
(Q10) [Q10定位词， anything else 来到该【属性priorities】的最后一点] Anything else?

59
00:02:56,996 --> 00:03:00,251
[Q10答案句] Well, I would like somewhere with a shared area.

60
00:03:00,251 --> 00:03:03,288
A TV room for example, or something like that.

61
00:03:03,288 --> 00:03:05,619
[Q10❗️ 听到socializing再蹲答案词已经晚了] It's a good way to socialise.

62
00:03:05,619 --> 00:03:06,574
It certainly is.

63
00:03:06,574 --> 00:03:07,833
That's it.

64
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:11,336
Now, we just need a contact telephone number for you.

65
00:03:11,336 --> 00:03:14,915
Sure, I'll just find it.

66
00:03:14,915 --> 00:03:19,823
It's double 67549.

67
00:03:19,823 --> 00:03:22,323
Great, so we'll be in contact with you as soon as possible…

